  "result": "I found and fixed the bug: `Cart.remove` was comparing the SKU you pass in against the item's **name** instead of its **SKU** (`shop/models.py:33`):\n\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.name != sku]\n```\n\n`'Widget' != 'sku-1'` is always true, so the Widget line was never removed. The SKU-keyed `add` method just above it already compares on SKU. I changed it to `l.item.sku != sku`.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, so only the Gadget line is left. Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest`: all 6 passed.\n\nNone of those tests call `Cart.remove`, so the suite would never have caught this bug. I can add a regression test for it if you want.",
